1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,577
In Session 4 you chose the first
automation for the leave request.

2
00:00:03,577 --> 00:00:05,434
Here it is, running in n8n.

3
00:00:05,434 --> 00:00:09,974
We will submit three requests: one
passes the checks, and two go to HR.

4
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:14,303
Each step in the Automation
lane becomes one node.

5
00:00:14,303 --> 00:00:16,009
The form is the trigger.

6
00:00:16,009 --> 00:00:19,016
Looking up the balance
is a Google Sheets node.

7
00:00:19,016 --> 00:00:23,277
The policy checks and the decision
are a code step and an IF.

8
00:00:23,277 --> 00:00:26,075
Logging and e-mails are Sheets and Gmail.

9
00:00:26,075 --> 00:00:28,989
And the manager's decision
stays with the manager.

10
00:00:30,130 --> 00:00:32,615
This is the workflow
right after importing it.

11
00:00:32,615 --> 00:00:36,690
The red triangles mean something is missing:
here, the Google credentials and the link to

12
00:00:36,690 --> 00:00:37,177
the sheet.

13
00:00:37,177 --> 00:00:40,300
Until they are filled in, the
workflow cannot be published.

14
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:43,460
The trigger is an n8n form.

15
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:49,010
It has two addresses: the test URL, which
listens while you test, and the production URL,

16
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:51,703
which works for everyone once
the workflow is published.

17
00:00:52,830 --> 00:00:57,729
Click Execute workflow, open the test form, and
submit a request: annual leave from the fifteenth

18
00:00:57,729 --> 00:00:59,053
to the seventeenth of November.

19
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:02,557
Open the form node and read its output.

20
00:01:02,557 --> 00:01:05,076
One submission is one
item, with seven fields.

21
00:01:05,076 --> 00:01:07,491
These fields are what the next nodes use.

22
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:12,227
The policy checks follow the leave
policy, one sentence at a time.

23
00:01:12,227 --> 00:01:16,581
One or two days of leave need two working
days of notice; three or more need ten.

24
00:01:16,581 --> 00:01:19,182
And the request must fit
the remaining balance.

25
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:23,373
The IF node asks one question:
did all checks pass?

26
00:01:23,373 --> 00:01:24,627
True goes to the manager.

27
00:01:24,627 --> 00:01:26,032
False goes to HR.

28
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:28,621
The first request passes.

29
00:01:28,621 --> 00:01:31,489
Every node turns green, with
one item on each arrow.

30
00:01:31,489 --> 00:01:35,204
The request is logged as pending, and
the manager receives a decision card.

31
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:41,205
Two more requests: one with only one day's
notice, and one asking for three days when only

32
00:01:41,205 --> 00:01:41,855
two remain.

33
00:01:41,855 --> 00:01:45,454
Both take the false path and
go to HR, not to the manager.

34
00:01:45,454 --> 00:01:49,575
On the left, the Executions list
keeps every run, with its data.

35
00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:55,470
And the sheet holds the record: one request
pending the manager, and two flagged for HR, each

36
00:01:55,470 --> 00:01:57,165
with its reason in plain words.

37
00:01:58,310 --> 00:02:00,295
Notice what the workflow does not do.

38
00:02:00,295 --> 00:02:04,336
It prepares, and it never approves or
declines: the manager still decides.

39
00:02:04,336 --> 00:02:08,202
A reminder comes later, and
Session 6 adds an AI step.

